# Force LF in the working tree on every platform, not just in the repository.
#
# This is load-bearing, not cosmetic. The UI5 build embeds the literal text of
# each .ts source into the `sourcesContent` field of its .js.map — as escaped
# "\r\n" or "\n" *inside a JSON string*. Git's usual eol normalisation never
# touches those, because they are escape sequences in a string, not line
# endings in the file.
#
# So a CRLF checkout (Windows default) produces a different dist/ than an LF
# checkout (Linux/CI). Since dist/ is committed and CI rebuilds it to verify
# freshness, that difference fails the build on the runner while looking clean
# on the developer's machine. Pinning eol=lf makes the build reproducible
# across platforms.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats must never be line-ending processed.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.tgz binary
